the late Queen Elizabeth began riding  horses at three years old her father  George VI gave Elizabeth her first  personal horse a bushy Maine  done-colored Shetland named Peggy when  she was four  George VI unabashedly lived up to the  cliche that racing is the sport of Kings  he sought bought and bred quality racing  thoroughbreds when he died in 1952  Elizabeth inherited George's equestrian  operation the Royal studs at Sandringham  Norfolk in addition to inheriting the  king's Stables of Runners hacking horses  and hunters and thus she began her  immersive seven decade Odyssey into the  equine world how passionate a horse  woman was she  despite kovid and her increasing frailty  the queen hadn't skipped a Royal Windsor  Horse Show since its Inception in 1943  when she had to forego her usual  Walkabout for medical reasons she still  went to the horse show The Queen Is  perhaps best known to the British racing  public for leading the annual  spectacularly formal Landau Carriage  parade at the Royal Ascot meeting each  June and for running many of her horses  in the various Stakes over the week  during her 70-year Reign Elizabeth  missed attending just one Royal Ascot  the 2022 meeting this past June  beginning in the mid-1980s the queen  began sending many of her breeding  Stables mares to Kentucky to be bred to  top American thoroughbreds which are  horses that are considered to have  greater speed than British Racers the  Queen's Monumental work ethic as Monarch  applied to her level of study and  Devotion to her horses especially the  breeding and racing operations  last year at 95 she was begged by her  doctors to step back from her own riding  but after the Platinum Jubilee  celebrations in early June she continued  to ride her horses  Elizabeth II didn't quit anything if she  could help it not philanthropy not  government not public appearances not  her Christmas speech and certainly not  racing her horses won all the British  Classics ascot's Gold Cup epsom's Derby  the lot and she's been inducted into the  British racing Hall of Fame as  calculated from 1988 until 2022 Queen  Elizabeth's racers in all classes and on  all surfaces won her 8.7 million pounds  or about 10 million US Dollars she  entered her horses in  3441 races in the last 35 years winning  566 of them her most successful year was  2021 when she won 36 races of the 166  she had her horses enter proving that  horse racing could very easily be known  as the sport of Queens  with a characteristically sharp eye on  the bottom line she gave a lot to the  sport but also made it hay  [Music]
 

